/src/scripts
# …but the OPERATIONAL scripts must ship: the backfills are deliverables the
# billing tickets require, and the CLI entry points are documented in
# docs/BILLING_RUNBOOK.md as the way to run and pause these jobs. An on-call
# runbook that references a script nobody else has is not a runbook.
#
# (The six scripts already tracked above this rule stay tracked because git
# ignores .gitignore for files already in the index — which is why this was not
# noticed sooner. New ones need an explicit negation.)
!/src/scripts/print-migrations.ts
!/src/scripts/backfill-default-payment-methods.ts
!/src/scripts/backfill-billing-transactions.ts
!/src/scripts/backfill-stale-cancellations.ts
!/src/scripts/check-ledger-gaps.ts
!/src/scripts/run-notification-jobs.ts
!/src/scripts/drain-email-outbox.ts
/claude reference
